# Copy this file to ".env" (same folder) and fill in real values there.
# ".env" is listed in .gitignore, so it is never uploaded to GitHub.
#
# The app does not need any keys today: it keeps its data on the phone.
#
# Later, when the app is connected to the Flex Daddies backend:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL is the address of the backend. Anything starting with
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_ is built INTO the app and can be read by anyone who has the
#   app, so only ever put public, non-secret values in those.
#   Real secrets (store upload keys, signing passwords) never go in this file
#   or in the app. They are stored by Expo with "eas credentials" / "eas env".
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=
